WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:02.730
Nobody saw these flicks coming.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:08.519
From an MCU darling trading his Avenger buds
in for some furry friends to a 21st century

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:13.589
take on a buzz-worthy horror classic, these
are just some of the most surprising, unexpected,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.120
and straight-up bizarre movies hitting theatres
in 2020.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.000
Dr. Dolittle is a character with a weird history.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.350
The physician who could talk with animals
was created by author Hugh Lofting in letters

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.320
written home to his children from the trenches
of World War I.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.169
The character would go on to become the star
of a series of popular children's books, set

00:00:31.169 --> 00:00:34.720
in Victorian England and published from the
1920s through the '50s.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.300
A number of adaptations appeared over the
following decades, including cartoons, radio

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.190
plays, stage productions, and a lavish 1967
movie musical starring Rex Harrison.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.070
When modern audiences see the name "Dolittle,"
however, they probably think back to the 1998

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.420
movie starring Eddie Murphy, which became
something of a franchise all its own, spawning

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.560
such intriguingly titled direct-to-DVD sequels
as Tail to the Chief.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:05.489
Now, the good doctor is returning to the big
screen in the form of… wait for it…

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:07.250
Robert Downey Jr.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:12.369
The animal cast will be voiced by a star-studded
lineup that includes Rami Malek, John Cena,

00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:18.329
Emma Thompson, Octavia Spencer, Tom Holland,
Selena Gomez, and Ralph Fiennes.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:22.229
We know exactly what you thinking: Where
in the world did this one come from?

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:26.320
We don't exactly have an answer for ya - but
after over a decade rocking that Iron-Man

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:30.040
suit, maybe RDJ just needed to lighten things
up a little bit.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.759
It is the destiny of all horror franchises
to be rebooted.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:37.990
That's been the case for pretty much the entire
21st century so far - since the dawn of the

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.520
new millennium, we've seen remakes and reimaginings
of The Texas Chainsaw Massacre, A Nightmare

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:48.609
on Elm Street, Friday the 13th, and multiple
stabs - pun intended - at a new Halloween.

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:50.250
"Please, dear god!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.960
Please!

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.520
Help me!

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.480
Please help me!"

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:59.030
Another long-dormant series seems ready for
similar treatment.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:04.390
Candyman, released in 1992, was based on a
story by Hellraiser creator Clive Barker and

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:09.360
starred Tony Todd as a supernatural killer
who haunted a housing project in Chicago and

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.080
represented the specter of racial and class
inequality.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.000
Also, bees came out of his mouth.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.500
It's weird and socially conscious and freaking
awesome.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.560
"She said his name the last time."

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.200
"Candyman."

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.560
"She turned out the lights."

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.920
And it's perfect material for the shockingly
prolific Jordan Peele, who is producing and

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.370
co-writing a new Candyman slated to hit theaters
in 2020.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:38.670
Bloody Disgusting reports that the film, directed
by up-and-comer Nia DaCosta, will be a "spiritual

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.440
sequel" that returns to the now-gentrified
neighborhood of the original.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:47.520
Casting remains unannounced, but Todd is angling
to be involved in some capacity.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.920
One of the most intriguing cinematic developments
of 2018 was the launch of Sony's new generation

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.480
of Spider-Man movies.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.510
Having successfully partnered with Marvel
to bring Tom Holland's live-action Peter Parker

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.810
to the MCU, the studio has set out to keep
their own stake in the Spidey brand alive

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.350
with a slate of spinoffs and animated titles.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:09.650
The first two examples, Venom and Into the
Spider-Verse, proved that they were ready

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.000
to explore a variety of unique and vastly
different facets of the webhead's corner of

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.170
the Marvel Universe.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:18.820
Work quickly began on sequels to both Venom
and Spider-Verse, though no firm dates for

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.070
those follow-ups have been officially announced.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:26.020
Sony has, however, confirmed a 2020 release
for Morbius, starring the, quote, "Living

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:30.200
Vampire" who has faced off with Spider-Man
in comics since the '70s.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.450
Nope - we didn't see that one coming either.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:38.290
Daniel Espinosa is on board to direct, with
a script by Dracula Untold writers Matt Sazama

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.460
and Burk Sharpless.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:44.900
Jared Leto will star as the titular bloodsucker,
with former Doctor Who actor Matt Smith appearing

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:50.840
in a major role and True Detective star Adria
Arjona as love interest Martine Bancroft.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:56.160
Coming to America was released in 1988, at
the height of Eddie Murphy's superstardom.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:01.560
Murphy, who co-wrote the story, stars as Prince
Akeem, heir to the throne of the fictional

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.720
African nation of Zamunda.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:07.250
Determined to escape an arranged marriage
and find a free-thinking bride to fall in

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:11.000
love with, he travels to New York City with
trusted aide Semmi in tow.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.139
It was a box office smash, capping off an
explosively successful decade for Murphy.

00:04:16.139 --> 00:04:17.389
"I've warned you.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.960
I'll be forced to thrash you."

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.640
"F--- you!"

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:29.400
After a period of rumors and rumblings, a
Coming to America sequel has been officially

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.629
announced and set to be released in 2020.

00:04:32.629 --> 00:04:38.219
You heard that right: Akeem is coming BACK
to America after 30 years, and this time he's

00:04:38.219 --> 00:04:40.379
searching for his long-lost son.

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:45.919
Original supporting players Arsenio Hall,
Shari Headley, John Amos, and James Earl Jones

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:48.099
are all rumored to be in talks as well.

00:04:48.099 --> 00:04:52.200
Black-ish creator Kenya Barris is penning
the screenplay, with Craig Brewer taking the

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.640
director's chair from the original movie's
John Landis.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:05:01.080
Not only are Roald Dahl's stories enduring
works of literature, they've also been adapted

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:07.020
by a staggeringly eclectic lineup of filmmakers
- Steven Spielberg, Tim Burton, Wes Anderson,

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.240
and Danny DeVito to name a few.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.150
In 2020, Robert Zemeckis will join that lineup
with a new take on The Witches.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:19.129
This 1983 children's novel tells the story
of an orphaned boy who goes to live with his

00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:20.919
grandmother, a retired witch hunter.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:25.210
The pair must battle an international coven
of witches poised to turn England's children

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.210
into mice.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:30.039
The Witches has been made into a movie once
before, in 1990.

00:05:30.039 --> 00:05:34.789
That production had a stellar array of talent,
with acclaimed director Nicolas Roeg at the

00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:39.449
helm, Jim Henson on board as producer, and
a delightfully wicked performance from Anjelica

00:05:39.449 --> 00:05:40.449
Huston.

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:44.569
The film was received enthusiastically by
critics, though Dahl, enraged by alterations

00:05:44.569 --> 00:05:47.960
to his story, called it "utterly appalling."

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.250
Zemeckis' Witches is already shaping up to
have an impressive pedigree of its own.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:56.409
Not only is the man behind Back to the Future
and Forrest Gump taking on writing and directing

00:05:56.409 --> 00:06:01.580
duties, but Guillermo del Toro and Alfonso
Cuarón are producing, and Anne Hathaway is

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.120
attached to star as the Grand High Witch.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:07.960
The Witches will enchant theaters in the 2020
Halloween season.

